# Part 1 - Libc functions 
  
- In this part you have to recreate some of the functions in the Libc library, your functions should have the same prototypes as the originals. 


* strlcat

Def:  is a size-bounded string concatenation function designed as a safer, less error-prone alternative to the traditional standard C library functions strcat() and strncat().


Prototype - size_t strlcat(char *dst, const char *src, size_t size);
